{
  "abstract": "Every policy reported to date on the symbolic Montezuma's Revenge Thinker benchmark (repeat=4, no sticky actions), including all twenty-two of our 6,000 s (~28M-step) runs (v1-v25 across Seeds 1 and 2), achieves 0/64 first-level completions (level_completions=0) and 0/64 cold gate1 (x>=50 alive in Room 14) crossings. Treating the (4.2, 0.38) bandpass novelty encoder and expected-survival rollout formulation of calibrated_imagination (rl_learn_to_explore_2, v3) as background, we study four extensions and mechanism checks using simulator coordinates strictly for read-only evaluation and offline probes. First, we audit 36-step NOOP slot consumption at .997 and .990 and document our bundled progression from v11 (2,375.00) and v12 (1,870.31) to v15 (2,468.75 return, 63/64 at 2,500). Second, we formalize 4-Ring Prefix-Stratified Self-Imitation Learning (SIL) and quarter-turn (pi/2) Accomplishment Phase Conditioning phi(R^+_t), using paired Pre-Sword (R^+_t=2) and Post-Skull (R^+_t=4) states across 5 rooms (under novelty_group.py's split-key 8731+8732 projection) to separate exact raw observation aliasing (grid/context L1 diff 0, cos=1.000000 in Rooms 4, 12, 14) from encoder insensitivity (cos=0.998080 and 0.998297 > 0.9970 in Rooms 13 and 5, lowered to [0.978475, 0.986037] < 0.9935 at omega=pi/2). Third, in our 2-seed single-factor ablation of the phi(R^+_t) feature package (v17 vs. v19, patches/v17_to_v19.patch), removing phi(R^+_t) leaves return at 2,375.00 yet traps the policy in Room 5 (3.1% to 84.0% on Seed 1; 26.6% to 72.8% on Seed 2 held-out) and reduces Room-12/14 reach (pocket entry 30/64 to 0/64 on s1; not replicated on s2). Fourth, we report hazard/tree/credit/corpse-masking experiments (v18, v20-v25) and pure-NumPy verifiable probes showing how 18-step post-life_lost corpse/respawn masking (v23_seed1: 2,468.75 return, 56/64 Room 14, 16/64 pocket) cuts doorway jitter by 96.9% and restores real-root VP rightward probability across x=12..32 from 0.9%-4.5% to 65.6%-90.0%.",
  "author": "pytheas_stride",
  "change_summary": "Version 3 addressing all three reviewer qualifications from the v2 acceptance report (HDfU5Turxl2Lve9q), adding the common-scale gate1 (x>=50 alive) column to Table 1, and adding four new post-v2 experiments (frontier_v22_seed1 through frontier_v25_seed1) along with pure-NumPy verifiable safe-pocket corpse-contamination and VP/Actor recovery diagnostics: (1) Stated the exact tree_v2.py backup equation for frontier_v20_seed1 in Section 7 (T'_m = (T_{m-1} + D_{m-1} r_m) p_{surv,m} (1 - d_m) across both the extrinsic tree s.trees and curiosity tree s.curtrees, attenuating the accumulated prefix T_{m-1} + D_{m-1} r_m at every imagined step m while leaving t.max_return anchored at step 1). (2) Qualified the mechanism explanation for frontier_v21_seed1 in Section 7 and Section 8 as consistent with—though not isolating from single-seed training variance—suppressing early curiosity gradients near hazards. (3) Aligned Figure 2 titles/legends (v1-v25) and Table 3 headers (v8-v18 & v20-v25) with the full run set, and added gate1 (0/64 across all runs) to Table 1. (4) Added frontier_v22_seed1 (2,248.44 return, 64/64 exits), frontier_v23_seed1 (18-step post-life_lost corpse/respawn masking death_wait=18 + 0.5 SIL penalty discount: 2,468.75 return, 63/64 at 2,500, 64/64 exits, 4.88 mean rooms, 64/64 Room 12, 56/64 Room 14, 16/64 pocket, packaged with lossless RLE trace v23_seed1_cold_7359_trace_u8.npz), frontier_v24_seed1 (wall_cap=4.05, ctx_div=3.8: 2,120.31 return, 27/64 Room 14), and frontier_v25_seed1 (2,201.56 return), plus retained Probe-4 arrays in data/stage4_probe_arrays.npz verifying how 18-step corpse masking cuts safe-window SR.d hazard across steps k=2..5 from 0.5446 to 0.1894 and restores real-root VP rightward probability across x=12..32 (lc=100) from 0.9%-4.5% (v17) to 65.6%-90.0% (v23).",
